        "original_id": "f257a79e-3118-5d75-b94f-775d37dbd163",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Aligarh Muslim University\n- Events: AMU Literary Festival\n- People: Mani Shankar Aiyar, Rajdeep Sardesai, Keki N. Daruwalla, Rana Ayyub\n- Roles: Indian diplomat, politician, Union Minister of Panchayati Raj, news anchor, author, poet, independent journalist\n\nFacts:\n- Mani Shankar Aiyar was born on 10 April 1941.\n- Mani Shankar Aiyar is a former Indian diplomat turned politician.\n- Mani Shankar Aiyar served as the Union Minister of Panchayati Raj until he lost his seat in the 2009 election.\n- AMU Literary Festival is an annual celebration of literature organized by Aligarh Muslim University, described as the Central University of India.\n- Previous invitees to AMU Literary Festival have included Rajdeep Sardesai, Keki N. Daruwalla, Mani Shankar Aiyar, and Rana Ayyub.\n- Rajdeep Sardesai is a news anchor and author.\n- Keki N. Daruwalla is a poet.\n- Rana Ayyub is an independent journalist.",
